{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhPRndeNXZFbYMY4t2qL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The regression is fixed: a stale worker can no longer finish, retry, delay or renew a job that another worker has recovered. The prevalidated regression command passes (7 files, 268 tests), and `npm run build` was re-run so the generated scripts match.\n\n## Cause\n\nThree Lua scripts checked only that *a* lock existed, not that it belonged to the caller's token:\n\n- **`src/commands/includes/removeLock.lua`** — now releases the lock only when the stored token equals the caller's. This helper gates complete, fail, immediate retry, delayed retry, move-to-wait and move-to-waiting-children, so all of them now reject a stale worker before touching anything.\n- **`src/commands/extendLock-2.lua`** — single-job renewal now requires the stored token to match, instead of overwriting the lock with the stale worker's token.\n- **`src/commands/extendLocks-1.lua`** — batch renewal has the same check per job; mismatched jobs come back in the failed-ID list.\n\nEach fix is a one-line change. No TypeScript changes were needed; the callers already passed tokens correctly.\n\n## Behaviour\n\n- **Stale operations:** rejected with the existing errors — `Lock mismatch for job …` (code -6) for the move operations, `0` from `extendLock`, and the job ID in the failed list from `extendLocks`.\n- **Missing locks:** still `Missing lock for job …` (code -2).\n- **Administrative calls:** the token `'0'` path that skips the lock check is untouched.\n- **Stalled-job recovery:** not changed.\n\n## Verification\n\nI added `tests/stale_worker_ownership.test.ts` with 7 tests. Each stale operation is checked to leave the job's state, hash fields (attempt counters, result), lock owner and event stream length unchanged, and then the real owner renews and finishes the job. Six of the seven fail on the original source and all pass with the fix; the seventh (missing lock) passes either way.\n\nExisting stalled-job, retry and backoff tests in the regression set pass.\n\nI did not run the rest of the test suite or the Postgres backend tests; the Postgres SQL already compares tokens, so I left it alone. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1073,"cache_read_input_tokens":54623,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1073},"output_tokens":693,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"191f61a1-f245-4c3a-b208-195b7f55d82c","uuid":"accb6d6e-3417-484c-a458-5bf87750faa4","timestamp":"2026-10-04T14:53:26.010Z","request_id":"req_011CfhPRmatfPk2wKUQwwYoR"}
